.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt WSIMRELAY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wsimrelay
.Nd carry a software radio's frames to a peer over UDP
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d Ar device
.Op Fl b Ar address
.Op Fl l Ar port
.Op Fl n Ar number
.Op Fl s Ar dbm
.Op Fl t Ar ms
.Ar peer
.Ar peer-port
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
opens
.Pa /dev/wsim ,
which gives it a software radio
.Pq Xr wsim 4 ,
and joins that radio to the radios of a peer in one medium: another
.Nm ,
on this machine or another, or the relay of a Linux guest whose
.Sy mac80211_hwsim
radios run hostapd.
It runs in the foreground until
.Dv SIGTERM
or
.Dv SIGINT ,
and then prints what it carried.
.Pp
Each frame the radio sends goes to
.Ar peer
at
.Ar peer-port
in one UDP datagram of version 1 of the relay format, which the kernel's
wireless Readme defines, and the peer's transmit status of it comes back
to the radio.
A frame with no status within the timeout fails, as one lost on the air
does.
Each frame from the peer goes to the radio, which receives it if it is
running, tuned to the frame's channel and its filters pass it, with the
signal
.Fl s
gives.
.Nm
answers the peer with the frame's status: no acknowledgement when none was
asked or the frame is group addressed, acknowledged when the radio
received a frame addressed to it, and failed otherwise.
Datagrams from any address but the peer's are ignored, whatever their
source port, since a forward of QEMU's user network sends from a port of
its own.
.Pp
Two relays on one machine join two of its radios, for checks that need
no Linux guest:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
wsimrelay -l 5550 127.0.0.1 5551 &
wsimrelay -l 5551 127.0.0.1 5550 &
.Ed
.Pp
The options:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d Ar device
The device, by default
.Pa /dev/wsim .
.It Fl b Ar address
The IPv4 address to bind, by default every address.
Between machines it is the address of a second card that
.Pa /etc/network/interfaces
and ifplugd leave alone, so that the medium outlasts a cable pulled
from eth0; beside the Linux AP guest that card is eth1 on 10.0.4.0/24,
and the peer 10.0.4.2 at the port the guest's script forwards.
.It Fl l Ar port
The UDP port to bind, by default 5550.
.It Fl n Ar number
The number the peer knows the radio by, by default 0.
.It Fl s Ar dbm
The signal of frames from the peer, from \-100 to \-1 dBm, by default
\-50, as
.Sy mac80211_hwsim
reports.
.It Fl t Ar ms
How long a frame waits for the peer's status, from 1 to 60000
milliseconds, by default 1000.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 after a signal, 1 when the device, the socket or the radio fails, and 2
for a usage error.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
At the start
.Nm
prints the radio's name and address, the peer and the port it bound, as
.Ql wsimrelay: wsim0 02:77:73:00:00:00: relaying to 127.0.0.1:5551 from 0.0.0.0:5550 ;
at the end the frames sent, the peer's frames received, the frames failed
for want of a status and the records refused.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wsim 4 ,
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
